<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile sells 10,815 short tons of aluminum.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile sells 10,815 short tons of aluminum.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Defense National Stockpile Center said it sold 10,815 short tons of primary aluminum to seven companies, with Glencore buying more than half.</p>
<p>Reynolds Metals bought 500 short tons at $1,480 a ton.</p>
<p>Hunter Douglas Metals bought 2,000 tons at $1,484 to $1,478.</p>
<p>Glencore bought 6,250 tons at $1,491 to $1,481.</p>
<p>Global Minerals &amp; Metals bought 1,000 tons at $1,488 to $1,483.</p>
<p>Mitsui &amp; Co bought 550 tons at $1,486.</p>
<p>Commercial Alloys bought 240 tons at $1,502.</p>
<p>Trans-World bought 275 tons at $1,484.</p>
<p>The next offering will be on August 5.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
